(731444, 77654, 5965, '<td valign="top">OK, I don''t get it. Man''s been around for eons before Christianity, so it can''t mean that reading the bible is man''s oldest habit. The hilighted passage is about crucificition, so are you saying violence and hatred are man''s oldest habits. I suppose an argument could be made for that, but it''s a pretty bleak outlook.</td>', 'OK, I don''t get it. Man''s been around for eons before Christianity, so it can''t mean that reading the bible is man''s oldest habit. The hilighted passage is about crucificition, so are you saying violence and hatred are man''s oldest habits. I suppose an argument could be made for that, but it''s a pretty bleak outlook.', '2004-05-22 13:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(731448, 76624, 21367, '<td valign="top">Great concept, great use of b/w.  Excelletly timed shot.  Crop may be a little tight for me (near the hammer head)...but high marks.</td>', 'Great concept, great use of b/w.  Excelletly timed shot.  Crop may be a little tight for me (near the hammer head)...but high marks.', '2004-05-22 13:56:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(731456, 76507, 21367, '<td valign="top">Us guys can spot this bad habit from a mile away...  IMO The crop and the location take away from this picture.  If you couldn''t capture this in a beach/pool environment, I might have thrown a blanket or beach towel out on the back lawn in a nice sunny area.  Have the subject laying face down maybe reading a book held by the right hand and the left hand picking the floss as you have here.  Take the shot from a tripod near the subjects feet and kind of catch the whole body and still keep the animinity by not catching the subjects face.  I would try to catch the dof where the hand/string are in focus but the rest of the pic a little fuzzy.   If you don''t have a lawn availbable this could have been done in a bedroom as if the subject was dressing for the beach/pool kind of thing.   Just my thoughts, I think it would be better with more objects in the picture.</td>', 'Us guys can spot this bad habit from a mile away...  IMO The crop and the location take away from this picture.  If you couldn''t capture this in a beach/pool environment, I might have thrown a blanket or beach towel out on the back lawn in a nice sunny area.  Have the subject laying face down maybe reading a book held by the right hand and the left hand picking the floss as you have here.  Take the shot from a tripod near the subjects feet and kind of catch the whole body and still keep the animinity by not catching the subjects face.  I would try to catch the dof where the hand/string are in focus but the rest of the pic a little fuzzy.   If you don''t have a lawn availbable this could have been done in a bedroom as if the subject was dressing for the beach/pool kind of thing.   Just my thoughts, I think it would be better with more objects in the picture.', '2004-05-22 14:19:45.000000', NULL, 1),
