(736798, 77371, 22011, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by stormy:</b></div><hr/><i> Yes it is a shower!  I am not too worried that I didn''t go well.  It is my first try and I think the photo is ok.  I don''t really mind if people do not understand me.  At least I didn''t pick my nose (hehe)  Thanks for the comments. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi-ho,<br/> <br/>What is the wee yellow thing then?  :-).<br/> <br/>If you included some more clues, like a bottle of shampoo, or a soap-on-a-rope behind the glass it would have been far more clear..  <br/> <br/>I wouldn''t worry about being new to this game, I just joined as well and I''m waiting the outcome of my first challenge attempt (Multiple Light sources).  Cross fingers.<br/> <br/>You''re right about the nose picking, I don''t think there is a good way to show that habit...<br/> <br/>edit: Typo<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-26 21:10:44.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by stormy: Yes it is a shower!  I am not too worried that I didn''t go well.  It is my first try and I think the photo is ok.  I don''t really mind if people do not understand me.  At least I didn''t pick my nose (hehe)  Thanks for the comments.   Hi-ho, What is the wee yellow thing then?  :-). If you included some more clues, like a bottle of shampoo, or a soap-on-a-rope behind the glass it would have been far more clear..   I wouldn''t worry about being new to this game, I just joined as well and I''m waiting the outcome of my first challenge attempt (Multiple Light sources).  Cross fingers. You''re right about the nose picking, I don''t think there is a good way to show that habit... edit: Typo', '2004-05-26 07:46:36.000000', '2004-05-26 22:10:44.000000', 0),
(736875, 77696, 18505, '<td valign="top">I feel compelled to respond to this one.  Meditation can be considered to be a habit by those who regularly and frequently practice the discipline.  In this case, the setting was important as it is a natural environment.  It is early spring here.  This particular spot is not in a swamp, but in the center of a ring of what will become tall bamboo later in the season.  Part of the point was that, as with any habit, meditation can be practiced wherever you happen to be.</td>', 'I feel compelled to respond to this one.  Meditation can be considered to be a habit by those who regularly and frequently practice the discipline.  In this case, the setting was important as it is a natural environment.  It is early spring here.  This particular spot is not in a swamp, but in the center of a ring of what will become tall bamboo later in the season.  Part of the point was that, as with any habit, meditation can be practiced wherever you happen to be.', '2004-05-26 09:08:50.000000', NULL, 0),
