(743326, 76854, 19672, '<td valign="top">To all the people who don''t think it fit the challenge...<br/> <br/>"Feeding the animals" is a bad habit...*sheesh*...I figured viewers would figure that out...next time I know it''s better to simply put it BLUNTLY in the title.<br/> <br/>We were in Balboa Park and every animal we came across my mom insisted on feeding. Sadly, i think a lot of people knocked me for this...<br/> <br/>Live and learn...sadly, my latest submission didn''t get finished until 10 minutes too late for submission into three...so being so annoyed at these stupid time restraints that keep killing my best photo submissions. I just submitted it to sports. Technically, it IS a sport....<br/> <br/>SWORDFIGHTING!!!<br/> <br/>Yeah, okay, so it''s not a modern sport but it was quite the popular team sport a few centuries back....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-31 17:07:19.</i></td>', 'To all the people who don''t think it fit the challenge... "Feeding the animals" is a bad habit...*sheesh*...I figured viewers would figure that out...next time I know it''s better to simply put it BLUNTLY in the title. We were in Balboa Park and every animal we came across my mom insisted on feeding. Sadly, i think a lot of people knocked me for this... Live and learn...sadly, my latest submission didn''t get finished until 10 minutes too late for submission into three...so being so annoyed at these stupid time restraints that keep killing my best photo submissions. I just submitted it to sports. Technically, it IS a sport.... SWORDFIGHTING!!! Yeah, okay, so it''s not a modern sport but it was quite the popular team sport a few centuries back....', '2004-05-31 01:28:18.000000', '2004-05-31 18:07:19.000000', 0),
(744272, 77496, 1368, '<td valign="top">Its a blue ribbon to me!<br/>Beautiful stuff :)</td>', 'Its a blue ribbon to me!Beautiful stuff :)', '2004-05-31 15:48:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(744802, 77337, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPChallenge!  I see this is your second challenge entry.  You have the right idea here, it''s a bad habit unless you win! ;)<br/> <br/>You got a lot of great comments during the challenge, most of them echoing what I would say.<br/> <br/>First, try coming from a higher angle or remove the cards in the background but I would like to see a different angle, bringing just the hand the money into the center of attention.  The back cards are very distracting.<br/> <br/>It''s a little bright, maybe tone down the light just a bit or use a reflector to bring the light without the glares.<br/> <br/>Other than that, not a bad idea!  If you do reshoot this I would love to see the new pictures!<br/> <br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>DNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Welcome to DPChallenge!  I see this is your second challenge entry.  You have the right idea here, it''s a bad habit unless you win! ;) You got a lot of great comments during the challenge, most of them echoing what I would say. First, try coming from a higher angle or remove the cards in the background but I would like to see a different angle, bringing just the hand the money into the center of attention.  The back cards are very distracting. It''s a little bright, maybe tone down the light just a bit or use a reflector to bring the light without the glares. Other than that, not a bad idea!  If you do reshoot this I would love to see the new pictures! Good Luck In Future Challenges! DeanndaDNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!', '2004-05-31 23:53:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(744812, 77483, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Ahhh, the one who took my favorite Strength Shot! ;)<br/> <br/>People Watching is a bad habit for some, a good habit for others and I think I know what you are going for here but it''s hard to pull off in public places, getting that shot that combines all the elements you want when they are all random to start with.  There is a lot of color and distracting elements in this shot.  Maybe taking it to black and white or sepia would help with that point of the shot.  Not sure what cropping you did but the woman on the right could be your focal as the one doing the watching, bring her into the shot more if possible?  And a slightly tighter crop on the left taking out the two men, just leaving the women?  The older one watching the younger one?  If you do any tweaking to this shot I would love to see the results!  Keep shooting, you''re getting better every time!<br/> <br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>DNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Ahhh, the one who took my favorite Strength Shot! ;) People Watching is a bad habit for some, a good habit for others and I think I know what you are going for here but it''s hard to pull off in public places, getting that shot that combines all the elements you want when they are all random to start with.  There is a lot of color and distracting elements in this shot.  Maybe taking it to black and white or sepia would help with that point of the shot.  Not sure what cropping you did but the woman on the right could be your focal as the one doing the watching, bring her into the shot more if possible?  And a slightly tighter crop on the left taking out the two men, just leaving the women?  The older one watching the younger one?  If you do any tweaking to this shot I would love to see the results!  Keep shooting, you''re getting better every time! Good Luck In Future Challenges! DeanndaDNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!', '2004-06-01 00:00:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(745347, 77398, 7969, '<td valign="top">hi greetings from the CC<br/>I like the diagonal line created in the shot by the hill.  Good use of depth of field in both foreground and background isolating the subject.  I think this was a hard challenge and you managed it fairly well from a tech point of view. Tho the shot lacks a little wow.   I think a horizontal format may have helped to give the viewer a bit more insight as to what you were shooting.  And perhaps had we even seen the photog.''s subject may have added a lil more umph to the shot.  This of course may also have been achieved by the fotog in shot stepping back a lil creating the illusion of more space on the right.  A tripod also may have helped to add a lil more of a dynamic.  Just some thoughts hope they help...happy shooting.</td>', 'hi greetings from the CCI like the diagonal line created in the shot by the hill.  Good use of depth of field in both foreground and background isolating the subject.  I think this was a hard challenge and you managed it fairly well from a tech point of view. Tho the shot lacks a little wow.   I think a horizontal format may have helped to give the viewer a bit more insight as to what you were shooting.  And perhaps had we even seen the photog.''s subject may have added a lil more umph to the shot.  This of course may also have been achieved by the fotog in shot stepping back a lil creating the illusion of more space on the right.  A tripod also may have helped to add a lil more of a dynamic.  Just some thoughts hope they help...happy shooting.', '2004-06-01 13:41:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(745350, 77232, 7969, '<td valign="top">HI greetings forom the CC.  This is not a bad portrait, tho I can see many thinking ''did not meet challenge''.  My biggest criticism would be the subjects glasses.  Primarily because as humans we see so much in a persons eyes, it is our way of connecting.  I would like to see it reshot without them.  Now I will ssay that the inclusion of them , does help the viewer to focus more on the lips and glass which is perhaps the point giving the context of the challenge topic.  <br/>The strongest feature of your shot IMO is the lighting, it is very well done on his face.  Thought the color is a little overexposed.   Just some thoughts...happy shooting</td>', 'HI greetings forom the CC.  This is not a bad portrait, tho I can see many thinking ''did not meet challenge''.  My biggest criticism would be the subjects glasses.  Primarily because as humans we see so much in a persons eyes, it is our way of connecting.  I would like to see it reshot without them.  Now I will ssay that the inclusion of them , does help the viewer to focus more on the lips and glass which is perhaps the point giving the context of the challenge topic.  The strongest feature of your shot IMO is the lighting, it is very well done on his face.  Thought the color is a little overexposed.   Just some thoughts...happy shooting', '2004-06-01 13:46:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(745353, 77343, 7969, '<td valign="top">Hi and greetings from the CC<br/>I like that you did not include the other tap, it makes for a little more interesting shot.   Generally a good shot in a hard challenge. I like that you chose a subject with interesting and older  hands.  The lighting seems a bit off somehow perhaps set for outdoors vs. indoors?  I would like to see it with the drainage hole PSed out perhaps (tho know u cant for this challenge) it is a little bit distracting.   I would also like to see this shot as a B&amp;W with a bit more contrast.  <br/>overall well done.  <br/>happy shooting.</td>', 'Hi and greetings from the CCI like that you did not include the other tap, it makes for a little more interesting shot.   Generally a good shot in a hard challenge. I like that you chose a subject with interesting and older  hands.  The lighting seems a bit off somehow perhaps set for outdoors vs. indoors?  I would like to see it with the drainage hole PSed out perhaps (tho know u cant for this challenge) it is a little bit distracting.   I would also like to see this shot as a B&W with a bit more contrast.  overall well done.  happy shooting.', '2004-06-01 13:50:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(747320, 77413, 7322, '<td valign="top">This got one of my higher scores (a 7). Partly, because it reminded me of my youngest daughter who does this constantly. I used to do it also but now I hardly ever paint my nails. Emotional responses aside I loved the bold red of her nails and the glass (is that a frozen daquiri?). You went beyond just showing a close-up of fingers and placed them in context. The fact that the contents of the glass she is holding is the same color red shows that you put some thought and care into the photo. Nice work!</td>', 'This got one of my higher scores (a 7). Partly, because it reminded me of my youngest daughter who does this constantly. I used to do it also but now I hardly ever paint my nails. Emotional responses aside I loved the bold red of her nails and the glass (is that a frozen daquiri?). You went beyond just showing a close-up of fingers and placed them in context. The fact that the contents of the glass she is holding is the same color red shows that you put some thought and care into the photo. Nice work!', '2004-06-02 14:50:55.000000', NULL, 0),
