(2394915, 76349, 50466, '<td valign="top">This would really be better if you reshoot and did a number of things. The firs tthing is to set your aperture at about f/8 and make sure the focus is spot on so as to get the best focus possible. Then, in photoshop, sharpen it ever so slightly and remove the yellowish cast by using either the channel mixer or colr balance. I really think this photo has a lot of potential and I appreciate the subtle message that it sends. Hope this helps some. <br/> <br/>Charles</td>', 'This would really be better if you reshoot and did a number of things. The firs tthing is to set your aperture at about f/8 and make sure the focus is spot on so as to get the best focus possible. Then, in photoshop, sharpen it ever so slightly and remove the yellowish cast by using either the channel mixer or colr balance. I really think this photo has a lot of potential and I appreciate the subtle message that it sends. Hope this helps some.  Charles', '2006-05-08 21:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2722446, 76178, 37961, '<td valign="top">Hmmm this is a great character study idea.</td>', 'Hmmm this is a great character study idea.', '2006-08-13 12:30:21.000000', NULL, 0),
